  "body": "https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-node-equals\r\n\r\nAt first thought it seems like you could check for sameness as a first step and return `true` early if possible. Are there any potential issues with such an approach? If so, could the reasoning be noted in the specification?\r\n\r\n- [WebKit does not check for sameness](https://github.com/WebKit/webkit/blob/9a8e6b0ca9a0cc5a0cfb0f7177526b217ea6ee75/Source/WebCore/dom/Node.cpp#L1256)\r\n- [Gecko does not check for sameness](https://github.com/mozilla/gecko-dev/blob/802e7b16f9ea42599aa6e03189babecfb49d6f9b/dom/base/nsINode.cpp#L991)\r\n\r\n",
